+# Final review: cluster evidence-hg-lnw-22
+
+Source: base 60e287aa, head 8f8ec538. Cluster files: five logs under evidence/hg-lnw.22/ (red-test_isolation, green-test_isolation, rebased-test_isolation, tier5-threads_real, rebased-tier5-threads_real). The cluster is log evidence only; I read the logs against bead hg-lnw.22 and the production change they back (commit 4327d3f, tests/threads_real.rs).
+
+## Evidence against the bead criteria
+
+- Red baseline: red-test_isolation.log shows 21 passed, 1 failed. The failure is test_sources_spawn_only_through_isolated_helpers, naming tests/threads_real.rs:50 rule R1 (raw std::process::Command::new). This matches the defect the bead describes exactly.
+- Green after fix: green-test_isolation.log and the rebased copy show 22 passed, 0 failed, including the lint test. At head, ThreadsDaemon::command in tests/threads_real.rs builds through support::private_herdr::private_command, so the spawn goes through the isolated helper.
+- Lint not loosened: the range diff of tests/test_isolation.rs is two assertions moving the pinned version string 3.1.0 to 3.6.0 in threads_binary_with_a_different_version_is_rejected. No scanner rule, allowlist or isolation-ok marker was added for threads_real.rs. The remaining isolation-ok markers are in tests/support/threads_bin.rs (version probe and cargo build) and predate this task.
+- Tier 5: tier5-threads_real.log and the rebased copy show 9 passed, 0 failed, exit=0, covering the adopt, rebind, resurrect-window and finalization scenarios. The first log is dominated by cold-cache compile output of the pinned herdr-threads 3.6.0 checkout (189s); the rebased run is warm (28s). Both are consistent.
+- The log header paths name the task worktree, so provenance is traceable. The test-binary hash is identical across red, green and rebased logs, which is expected since it is a metadata hash, not a content hash.
+
+## Gaps in the evidence
+
+- The logs do not show the command line, so the private-herdr feature flag and the hg-build toolbox are not evidenced by the logs themselves. The bead criterion names `--features private-herdr` in hg-build. Test names such as helper_*_private_herdr running imply the feature is on.
+- No leak check output (the AGENTS.md pgrep count) is captured for either run. The criterion "no rig leak" is asserted but not shown.
+- The requirement baseline section is absent from the root spec, so the baseline paragraph does not apply.
+
+## Verdict
+
+ready
+
+## Must fix before landing
+
+- none
+
+## Untested scope
+
+- The "no rig leak" criterion has no captured post-run leak-count output in evidence/hg-lnw.22; the logs only show passing tests.
+- The logs do not record the exact cargo invocation, so the private-herdr feature and hg-build toolbox use are inferred from test names, not shown.
+
